From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 06:52:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] squash! fonts: Report the load state of @font-face rules in
 FontFace.status

Restore the expectations of css/css-fonts/font-variant-emoji-2.html and
css/css-fonts/matching/font-unicode-presented-as-emoji-outline.html, which
that patch removed as stale.

They are not stale: both tests fail on Servo whenever a colour emoji font is
installed, which is the case on the CI runners of this fork and of upstream
alike, and upstream carries the same `expected: FAIL` for both. They only pass
in a container without an emoji font, which is what the patch was validated
in, so removing them made every CI run of this fork report two stable
unexpected failures that upstream does not see.

The restored files are byte-identical to upstream's, so nothing here diverges
from upstream any more.

Squash candidate: fold into the FontFace.status patch at the next sync.

Validation: with fonts-noto-color-emoji installed (the CI configuration, which reproduces the CI failures) `./mach test-wpt --release css/css-fonts/font-variant-emoji-2.html css/css-fonts/matching/font-unicode-presented-as-emoji-outline.html` reports both as expected; both also fail with an upstream-only release build, and the two files match `upstream/main` exactly.
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; root-caused and written by the agent)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
---
 tests/wpt/meta/css/css-fonts/font-variant-emoji-2.html.ini      | 2 ++
 .../matching/font-unicode-presented-as-emoji-outline.html.ini   | 2 ++
 2 files changed, 4 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 tests/wpt/meta/css/css-fonts/font-variant-emoji-2.html.ini
 create mode 100644 tests/wpt/meta/css/css-fonts/matching/font-unicode-presented-as-emoji-outline.html.ini

diff --git a/tests/wpt/meta/css/css-fonts/font-variant-emoji-2.html.ini b/tests/wpt/meta/css/css-fonts/font-variant-emoji-2.html.ini
new file mode 100644
